+- Press `ctrl+r` rename, `ctrl+t` pin, `ctrl+s` interrupt turn (PTY) / stop run, `d` mark done, `m` multi-select, `ctrl+x` delete/archive, `X` delete inactive rows in the selected state, and `?` for help.
+
+While attached, **Ctrl+] is reserved by Board** and always detaches, including with a draft or pending dialog; neither is cleared or answered. Left is only an empty-editor convenience. Ctrl+G is forwarded to Pi. This overrides Pi's default `tui.editor.jumpForward` (Ctrl+]) while attached; if you need character-jump, assign that Pi action another chord in your agent directory's `keybindings.json`. Board does not change your Pi bindings or offer a configurable detach chord.
+
+Ctrl+S on a hosted PTY requests an interrupt; it does not close the session or confirm that a turn has stopped. Mark done remains a semantic label, not host termination. Help (`?`) wraps to terminal width and scrolls with Up/Down, PageUp/PageDown, and Home/End; Escape returns.
 
 Rows are stored under `~/.pi/agent/agent-board/` by default. Deleting a row archives it from the board; it does not remove the underlying Pi session file.
 
+## Attention and inspection
+
+Board projects separate facts: `working` means producer state says alive and working,
+not merely that an idle PTY host exists. `decision` counts rows with an explicit
+cooperative owner-decision span, never inferred questions, unread output or generic
+custom UI. `new` counts rows with finalized non-tool-calling assistant text whose
+current response marker has not been visited. Tool starts/results and tool-calling commentary
+do not create a response marker. Terminal admin handoff and generic native UI
+waiting have separate `terminal` and `ui` labels; neither means approval is needed.
+These are advisory, row-level counts, not a worker roster or execution authority.
+
+Acknowledgement means focused VISIT, not proof of reading. Peek/transcript
+visits a captured response snapshot only after focused rendering with body space.
+Native PTY attach implements the installed TUI `Focusable.focused` contract and
+visits only after connected output has rendered successfully while focused.
+There are no manual mark keys or revision/action banners. Reply input is ordinary.
+
+Callbacks capture `{id, revision}` and the focus generation, never latest state.
+Blur/disposal invalidates deferred presentation even if focus returns immediately.
+Selection, prewarm, evidence, attach request, loading, failed render, background
+render, disconnect, settlement and exit do not acknowledge. Hidden late output
+under a parent modal stays new until the restored focused presentation renders;
+live focused arrivals clear on a subsequent render. Failed writes stay retryable
+on ordinary later renders, without a redraw spin or owner action requirement.
+Footer failures explicitly report stale/unavailable instead of old counts.
+
+PTY bytes and metadata have no shared response-ID boundary. Formatting, clipping,
+scrolling and timing do not prove whole-body visibility or textual reading.
+Supported native modal stacking drives focus, but generic custom UI has varied
+focus/overlay behavior; Board does not fake all dialogs as decisions or claim
+all custom surfaces blur/hide it. Cooperative decision spans remain independent.
+
+Producers own `state.json` and persist `{id, revision}` response markers. Consumers
+create empty private files in `acknowledgements/`, named by revision and SHA-256
+of response ID, with exclusive atomic create. These immutable exact markers form
+a monotonic set: concurrent and older writes cannot erase newer acknowledgements
+or acknowledge a different ID. Readers probe only the current response's path,
+not the directory: constant read cost as history grows. No locks, PID recovery,
+producer writes or mutable aggregate are involved; a writer dying after create
+leaves a complete marker. One empty file per visited response
+remains until the view is deleted; there is no pruning/compaction protocol.
+Legacy `acknowledgement.json` and abandoned locks are ignored, not migrated or
+deleted; a focused visit may be required again. No text or decision data
+is stored in these markers. Revisions survive foreground events and new runs;
+IDs disambiguate same-clock responses. Legacy timestamps invent no responses.
+This is local workspace state, not synchronized fleet delivery evidence.
+
+Decision tools may emit `pi.events.emit("owner:decision", {category, phase, id})`.
+The supported categories are `ask_user`, `admin_approval`, and `admin_terminal`;
+phases are balanced `start`/`end`, with a content-free opaque ID (1-128 ASCII
+letters, digits, hyphen or underscore). Board allowlists exactly these fields.
+The sender must use `finally`, covering an entire select-to-editor exchange, not
+just individual dialogs. Explicit spans work inside coalesced/nested native
+modals. A generic custom component is never an owner decision. Shutdown/reload
+clears cooperative spans and disposes listeners; no question, options, argv,
+answer or tool-result contents are added to attention records. Normal native
+session transcripts remain native Pi behavior, not an attention privacy store.
+Without a cooperative sender, Board does not guess an owner decision from tool
+names or dialogs. This is observation, never an approval bypass.
+
+The ordinary inline controller refreshes peer counts once per second while quiet;
+there is no factory-time or hosted-child refresh timer, and shutdown/reload clears
+it. Standalone/default instances retain event-driven footer updates. Dashboard
+polling uses the existing bounded controller loop. No model/auth/provider/root
+changes or extra orchestration are needed for attention.
+
 ## Configuration
 
 Useful environment variables:
 
 | Variable | Use |
 | --- | --- |
+| `AGENT_BOARD_COMPACT=1` | Opt-in compact dashboard: session/state/context header and essential footer; hides routine version/healthy transport summaries while retaining compact working/decision/new counts. Default off. Details remain under Space, `e`, `!`, and `?`; transport warnings remain visible. Narrow headers show the context folder name; Space shows its full path. |
 | `AGENT_BOARD_ROOT` | Store location. Defaults to `~/.pi/agent/agent-board/`. |
 | `AGENT_BOARD_AUTO_STATE=off` | Disable automatic terminal-state moves. |
 | `AGENT_BOARD_AUTO_STATE_MODEL=<model>` | Model for classifying finished turns. Defaults to `gpt-4o`; use `off` for heuristic-only. |
